<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Croatian–Hungarian Settlement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1868</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Nagodba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Croatian–Hungarian Settlement, or Nagodba, was the agreement of 1868 that defined the place of Croatia-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonia">Slavonia</a> within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">Austro-Hungarian Compromise of 1867</a>. Croatia-Slavonia kept its own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatian-parliament">Sabor</a> and control of internal affairs, justice, education and religion, under a ban appointed on the Hungarian prime minister's advice, while finance, defence and other common affairs were handled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/croatian-hungarian-settlement.jpg" alt="Croatian–Hungarian Settlement" width="320" height="351" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roberta. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rijecka_krpica_HDA_300109.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
